[32m+[m[32m## What's new in 0.5[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 1. Exploits that complete the lab objective[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Direct-exploit mode** — you already know the lab's vulnerable endpoint?[m
[32m+[m[32m  Point the exploit engine straight at it and it runs the full chain[m
[32m+[m[32m  (UNION extraction → credential dump → automatic login → account takeover),[m
[32m+[m[32m  regardless of what the crawler/detector found:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```bash[m
[32m+[m[32m  bughound scan https://lab.web-security-academy.net/ \[m
[32m+[m[32m      --authorize-host lab.web-security-academy.net --i-am-authorized \[m
[32m+[m[32m      --aggressive \[m
[32m+[m[32m      --exploit-endpoint 'https://lab.web-security-academy.net/filter?category=Pets' \[m
[32m+[m[32m      --exploit-param category[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Broader lab dialect support**: Oracle (`FROM dual`, `v$version`,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `all_tables`/`all_tab_columns`, `LISTAGG`) and MSSQL (`@@version`,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `FOR XML PATH` enumeration) joined SQLite / MySQL / PostgreSQL for UNION and[m
[32m+[m[32m  blind extraction.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **More reliable UNION shape discovery**: candidate column counts are now[m
[32m+[m[32m  validated by reflecting a unique marker through a string column, so[m
[32m+[m[32m  suppressed-error endpoints can no longer lock the search onto a wrong count.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Findings the detector missed as re-targetable are no longer dropped: the[m
[32m+[m[32m  exploit engine reconstructs a request target from the finding and still[m
[32m+[m[32m  attempts the chain.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The console prints a dedicated **Exploit results** block at the end of the[m
[32m+[m[32m  scan (one ✓ line per successful exploit), so exploitation status is[m
[32m+[m[32m  impossible to miss.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2. False-positive verification (control experiments)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEvery finding that the exploit phase could **not** prove is re-tested by[m
[32m+[m[32m`bughound/verification.py` with a battery of control experiments, and the[m
[32m+[m[32mreport answers "how do we know this is not a false positive?" with the actual[m
[32m+[m[32mresults:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Check | What it proves |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| `negative-control` | a payload with the active ingredient removed (no quote, no operator, no traversal...) does **not** trigger the signature — so the signature is input-specific, not page noise |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `repeat-consistency` | the signature reproduces on every repeat request — real injection is deterministic; rotating banners and A/B content are not |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `baseline-clean` | the unmodified request shows no signature |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `fresh-canary-*` | reflection findings are re-tested with a unique random canary per check — stale markers can never fake a reflection |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `directionality` | for boolean SQLi, TRUE must resemble baseline and FALSE must differ — in that direction only |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `timing-jitter` | for time-based SQLi, baseline network jitter is small enough to trust the delay signal |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFindings that pass everything get a **LOW false-positive risk** verdict; any[m
[32m+[m[32mfailed check **downgrades** the finding (`verified=False`, `confidence=[m
[32m+[m[32mtentative`) and prints a FAIL row in the report's *False-positive analysis*[m
[32m+[m[32mtable. A succeeded exploit is its own FP disproof and bypasses the battery.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 3. Reports that show WHERE the vulnerability lives[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **`--source-dir <path>`**: give it the application's source code and every[m
[32m+[m[32m  finding is mapped to the exact **file + line range + enclosing function +[m
[32m+[m[32m  sink line** (marked with `->`) — e.g. `os.popen(f"ping -c 1 {host}")` at[m
[32m+[m[32m  `examples/vulnerable_app.py:280`, inside `ping()`.[m
[32m+[m[32m  Supports FastAPI/Flask-style decorators, Express/Node routes, Spring[m
[32m+[m[32m  mappings, and PHP `$_GET` usage; sinks detected include SQL execute,[m
[32m+[m[32m  shell exec, file read, server-side fetch, redirect and raw echo.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **No source available?** (black-box lab) Each finding instead carries a[m
[32m+[m[32m  clearly-labelled **reconstructed sink pattern** — the shape of code the[m
[32m+[m[32m  input provably reaches, derived from the captured behavioural evidence[m
[32m+[m[32m  (quote breaks query, tautology changes result set, command output echoes...).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Every finding also shows its **injection point**[m
[32m+[m[32m  (e.g. `GET /filter?category=... -> query-string parameter 'category'`).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Methodology appendix documents the verification and code-attribution steps.[m
