[32m+[m[32m## Exploitation & proof (0.4 features, extended in 0.5)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDetection alone tells you "something looks wrong". bughound's **exploit phase**[m
[32m+[m[32m(runs automatically in aggressive mode) goes further: every detected finding is[m
[32m+[m[32mre-targeted with a **safe, non-destructive exploit** that demonstrates the[m
[32m+[m[32mactual impact — and for SQLi that means **completing the attack objective**,[m
[32m+[m[32mnot just proving an error:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Finding class | Exploit proof attempted |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Error-based SQLi | Adaptive UNION extraction (column count + quote-context + string-column discovery): DB version banner, table list, **then real credential rows from any users/credential table** |[m
[32m+[m[32m| UNION with credentials | **Automatic login** through the application's own login form with the extracted credentials → **ACCOUNT TAKEOVER** proof (failed-login baseline comparison, session markers) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Hidden data | Tautology injection (`' OR 1=1--`) that makes filtered-out records reappear — proven by measuring content growth beyond payload reflection |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Boolean-blind SQLi | Character-by-character binary-search extraction of **a privileged user's password** (length + chars, hash auto-cracking), falling back to the DB version banner |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Blind + extracted password | **Automatic login** → **ACCOUNT TAKEOVER** proof |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Cookie SQLi (TrackingId-style) | Cookies are treated as injectable parameters end-to-end: detected, UNION-probed, blind-extracted — with the cookie override isolated to single requests |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Time-based SQLi | Boolean-oracle upgrade probe, then extraction when possible |[m
[32m+[m[32m| OS command injection | Runs `id` / `uname -sr` / `hostname` and captures the output — proves RCE **and which user** |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Path traversal / LFI | Reads `/etc/passwd` (accounts listed) plus a second distinct file to prove the read is arbitrary |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Reflected XSS | Verifies `<script>`, `onerror=`, `svg onload=` payloads survive unfiltered in an HTML context (content-type aware) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| SSRF | Makes the target fetch **its own loopback address** and return its content — proves server-side fetching with data exfiltration |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Open redirect | Walks and documents the full redirect chain (hop-by-hop) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| NoSQL operator injection | Attempts a real authentication bypass via `[$ne]` and detects authenticated-page markers |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Everything else | Gets a curl repro + raw HTTP exchange + impact statement + manual steps |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Every exploited finding lands in the report with:**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- ✅ **EXPLOITED** badge and an executive-summary count,[m
[32m+[m[32m- the **data extracted from the target** (DB banner, table names, **credential[m
[32m+[m[32m  rows**, `/etc/passwd` lines, `uid=...` output, loopback fingerprints...),[m
[32m+[m[32m- the **account-takeover proof** when extracted credentials successfully[m
[32m+[m[32m  logged into the application (objective completion, not just a read),[m
[32m+[m[32m- a **ready-to-run `curl` reproduction** (copy-paste, works as-is),[m
[32m+[m[32m- the **verbatim raw HTTP request/response exchange** (Burp-style),[m
[32m+[m[32m- numbered **manual reproduction steps** for triagers,[m
[32m+[m[32m- a written **impact statement** per vulnerability class,[m
[32m+[m[32m- the **Vulnerable code location** section (source-mapped sink or[m
[32m+[m[32m  behaviour-derived reconstruction),[m
[32m+[m[32m- the **False-positive analysis** section (control-experiment table + verdict).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen an exploit *cannot* be completed, the report says so honestly[m
[32m+[m[32m(`Exploit phase result: ...`) and the finding keeps its detection-stage[m
[32m+[m[32mevidence and confidence label — bughound never upgrades a finding it could[m
[32m+[m[32mnot prove.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Safety rules of the exploit phase** (all enforced in code):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Requires `--aggressive` **and** the normal authorization gate; disable[m
[32m+[m[32m  independently with `--no-exploit` (CLI) or `"exploit": false` (web API).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Strictly read-only / informational payloads: SQL extraction of metadata and[m
[32m+[m[32m  credential rows, `id`/`uname`, system-file reads, marker reflections, and[m
[32m+[m[32m  logins **using credentials the target itself leaked** (at most 2 attempts —[m
[32m+[m[32m  a failed-login baseline plus the extracted credential — never brute-force).[m
[32m+[m[32m  No data is modified, no destructive or denial-of-service payloads exist in[m
[32m+[m[32m  the codebase.[m
[32m+[m[32m- SSRF proofs target **loopback / the target itself only** — cloud metadata[m
[32m+[m[32m  endpoints (169.254.169.254 etc.) are hard-blocked.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Every exploit request flows through the same denylist-guarded HTTP client[m
[32m+[m[32m  as the rest of the scan; cookie-override probes are restored immediately[m
[32m+[m[32m  so the scanner's own session is never polluted.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Per-finding request budgets keep the phase fast and gentle.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA full example report produced against the bundled vulnerable demo app is in[m
[32m+[m[32m[`examples/sample-report.md`](examples/sample-report.md).[m
