[32m+[m[32m### Troubleshooting: "0 URLs discovered" / no findings[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf a scan finishes almost instantly with `Discovered 0 URLs, 0 injectable[m
[32m+[m[32mtargets` and no findings, the target was unreachable. bughound now does a[m
[32m+[m[32msingle pre-flight GET before crawling and emits the exact failure reason:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mbughound scanning https://lab.web-security-academy.net/ (aggressive mode, timeout=30.0s)[m
[32m+[m[32m[08:39:12] Probing target https://lab.web-security-academy.net/ (timeout 30.0s)...[m
[32m+[m[32m[08:39:42]   initial probe failed: ConnectTimeout:[m
[32m+[m[32m             retrying once with 2x timeout (target may be waking up)...[m
[32m+[m[32m[08:40:12] Target unreachable -- aborting scan (see report for details).[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCommon fixes (in order of likelihood for online labs / shared-hosting[m
[32m+[m[32mtargets):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Open the URL in your browser first.** PortSwigger Web Security Academy[m
[32m+[m[32m   labs, AWS Lambda, and similar on-demand runtimes go to sleep after[m
[32m+[m[32m   inactivity. The first request wakes them up but can take >15s; once awake[m
[32m+[m[32m   subsequent requests are fast.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Increase the timeout:** `--timeout 60` (default is now 30s; was 15s).[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Override the User-Agent:** `--user-agent 'Mozilla/5.0 ...'`. The[m
